course: dictionary
lesson: 16101
title: Weatherman
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Use the words around a new word as clues. The word weatherman has two parts you can spot: weather and man. Weather is what the sky does, and a man is a man, so the word is about a man and the weather.
explain: «The weatherman said it would rain on Saturday, so we took umbrellas.» The words said, rain and umbrellas tell you the weatherman talks about the weather. A weatherman tells people what the weather will be, so this clue fits well.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The man who tells us the weather said it would rain on Saturday, so we took umbrellas.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A weatherman is a noun. One is a weatherman, and more than one is weathermen.
fact: «Weatherman» means a man who tells people what the weather will be, especially on TV or radio.
fact: Informally, a weatherman can mean any weather forecaster, which is a person who predicts the weather.
fact: A meteorologist is a scientist who studies weather. Some meteorologists work as weathermen on TV.
exercise: «The weatherman said it would be sunny all week.» What is a weatherman? | A type of raincoat | A kind of cloud | A person who makes the weather happen | *A person who tells people what the weather will be
exercise: What is the plural of weatherman? | weathers | weathermans | weatherman's | *weathermen
exercise: Which word means a scientist who studies weather? | Geologist | Biologist | *Meteorologist | Astronomer
test: «Dad watched the weatherman on the news before he packed the car.» Why did Dad watch the weatherman? | To check the football score | To learn a new dance | To buy a new car | *To find out what the weather would be
test: «The weatherman forecast snow for Friday.» What is he most likely doing? | Cooking the snow | *Telling people what the weather will be | Painting a house | Driving a bus
exam: Which is the correct plural of weatherman? | weatherwomans | weathermans | *weathermen | weatherman
